"US":[{"t":"plan","n":"Local zoning and planning rules","b":"Zoning and planning officials of state, local, tribal and territorial governments","u":"https://www.fema.gov/sites/default/files/documents/fema_p-2196-building-codes-adoption-playbook-for-authorities-having-jurisdictions.pdf","x":"FEMA P-2196 (2025): the authorities having jurisdiction include zoning, planning, building, fire and floodplain officials who decide how or where buildings are built. Check the zoning code of the city or county of the site.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"gov","n":"Building codes adopted and enforced by state and local governments","b":"Authorities having jurisdiction (AHJs) at state, local, tribal and territorial level","u":"https://www.fema.gov/sites/default/files/documents/fema_p-2196-building-codes-adoption-playbook-for-authorities-having-jurisdictions.pdf","x":"Most construction rules in the United States come from each state and local government. AHJs adopt and enforce building codes and may amend them by ordinance. Check the code edition adopted where the project is.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"eng","n":"State licensure of professional engineers (P.E.)","b":"68 state and territory engineering licensing boards; NCEES","u":"https://ncees.org/licensure","u2":"https://ncees.org/ncees-services/records-program","x":"Only a licensed engineer can prepare, sign, seal and submit engineering drawings. NCEES members are the licensing boards of the 50 states, DC and 4 territories. Requirements vary by state; all state boards accept an NCEES Record.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"arch","n":"State licensure of architects","b":"State architecture licensing boards; NCARB (55 jurisdictions)","u":"https://www.ncarb.org/","x":"Each of NCARB's 55 jurisdictions sets its own licensing requirements. The NCARB Certificate helps architects apply for licenses in other states. NCARB recently updated its Competency Standard for Architects.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"fire","n":"NFPA 101 Life Safety Code","b":"National Fire Protection Association (NFPA)","u":"https://www.nfpa.org/codes-and-standards/nfpa-101-standard-development/101","x":"Current edition 2027. Covers life safety in new and existing buildings. Check which edition the local authority uses. Fire protection on construction sites: OSHA 29 CFR 1926 Subpart F.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"elec","n":"NFPA 70 National Electrical Code (NEC)","b":"NFPA; adopted by states and local authorities","u":"https://www.nfpa.org/codes-and-standards/nfpa-70-standard-development/70","x":"Current edition 2026. NFPA says the NEC is enforced in all 50 states. The adopted edition differs by state, so check the local edition. Electrical safety on construction sites: OSHA 29 CFR 1926 Subpart K.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"osh","n":"OSHA Safety and Health Regulations for Construction (29 CFR 1926)","b":"Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA), U.S. Department of Labor","u":"https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1926","x":"Subparts include C general provisions, F fire protection, K electrical, L scaffolds, Q concrete and masonry, R steel erection, AA confined spaces and CC cranes and derricks.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"env","n":"National Environmental Policy Act (NEPA): review of federal agency proposals","b":"Each federal agency under its own NEPA procedures","u":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/02/24/2026-03708/national-environmental-policy-act-implementing-regulations","u2":"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/01/ceq-fixes-decades-long-permitting-failure-through-deregulation","x":"CEQ removed its government-wide NEPA regulations (interim rule in effect 11 April 2025, final rule 8 January 2026). Each agency now applies its own procedures, for example the Department of the Interior rule of 24 February 2026.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"std","n":"ICC International Codes (I-Codes): model building codes","b":"International Code Council (ICC)","u":"https://www.fema.gov/sites/default/files/documents/fema_p-2196-building-codes-adoption-playbook-for-authorities-having-jurisdictions.pdf","x":"The flagship ICC model codes include the International Building Code (IBC) and the International Existing Building Code (IEBC). They reference national consensus and engineering standards. Use the edition the local AHJ adopted.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1}],
"VN":[{"t":"plan","n":"Law on Urban and Rural Planning No. 47/2024/QH15","l":"Luật Quy hoạch đô thị và nông thôn số 47/2024/QH15","b":"Ministry of Construction (Bộ Xây dựng)","u":"https://moc.gov.vn/pl/pages/ChiTietVanBan.aspx?TypeVB=0&vID=275","u2":"https://moc.gov.vn/pl/tin-tuc/460/tai-lieu-gioi-thieu-luat-sua-doi-bo-sung-mot-so-dieu-cua-luat-quy-hoach-do-thi-va-nong-thon-luat-so-1442025qh15.aspx","x":"Issued 26 November 2024, in force 1 July 2025. Brings urban and rural planning into one law. Amended by Law No. 144/2025/QH15, passed 12 November 2025.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"gov","n":"Construction Law No. 135/2025/QH15","l":"Luật Xây dựng số 135/2025/QH15","b":"Ministry of Construction (Bộ Xây dựng)","u":"https://moc.gov.vn/pl/Pages/chitiettin.aspx?IDNews=461&tieude=tai-lieu-gioi-thieu-luat-xay-dung-so-1352025qh15.aspx","u2":"https://maa.gov.vn/uploads/document/bx0qz0itjaztvs7-390-luat-xay-dung.pdf","x":"Passed 10 December 2025, in force 1 July 2026; some clauses (Article 43 clauses 2 and 3, Article 71, Article 95 clauses 3 to 5) from 1 January 2026. Replaces the Construction Law 2014.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1},
{"t":"fire","n":"Law on Fire Prevention, Fighting and Rescue No. 55/2024/QH15","l":"Luật Phòng cháy, chữa cháy và cứu nạn, cứu hộ số 55/2024/QH15","b":"Construction specialist agencies check fire safety acceptance (Ministry of Construction guidance)","u":"https://maa.gov.vn/van-ban/luat-n7zjj7kql9/luat-phong-chay-chua-chay-va-cuu-nan-cuu-ho-luat-so-55-2024-qh15-222.html","x":"Issued 29 November 2024, in force 1 July 2025; the Fire Law 27/2001 ended on that date. Fire alarm signals must connect to the national fire database by 1 July 2027 at the latest.","c":"2026-11-03","o":1}],
